* Names a macro's expansion defines by equ (Bit Hi: mHi equ 1<<.), in a moveq or move.b
* immediate: both Microware assemblers know their values there and take the byte (moveq #mHi
* with 128 is $80, move.b #^mLo $00FE); the translation didn't (gas expands the macros):
* "operands mismatch" for the moveqs, $FFFE for the complement. An external of the same kind
* (moveq #Ext) relocated as before.
* expect text: 7680 7081 74c8 177c00fe0001 123c0080 7800 4e71
 psect macro_equ_imm,0,0,0,0,0
Bit macro
m\1 equ 1<<.
b\1 do.b 1
 endm
Num macro
q\1 equ \2
 endm
 org 7
 Bit Hi
 org 0
 Bit Lo
 Num Big,200
 moveq #mHi,d3
 moveq #(mHi+mLo),d0
 moveq #qBig,d2
 move.b #^mLo,1(a3)
 move.b #mHi,d1
 moveq #Ext,d4
 nop
 ends
